WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Luke, Chapter Twenty-Two.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.533
Now the feast of unleavened bread drew nigh, which is called the Passover.

3
00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:11.733
And the chief priests and scribes sought how they might kill him; for they feared the people.

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:17.333
Then entered Satan into Judas surnamed Iscariot, being of the number of the twelve.

5
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:23.467
And he went his way, and communed with the chief priests and captains, how he might betray him unto them.

6
00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.533
And they were glad, and covenanted to give him money.

7
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:31.733
And he promised, and sought opportunity to betray him unto them in the absence of the multitude.

8
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:36.267
Then came the day of unleavened bread, when the passover must be killed.

9
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:41.467
And he sent Peter and John, saying, Go and prepare us the passover, that we may eat.

10
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.333
And they said unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare?

11
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:54.667
And he said unto them, Behold, when ye are entered into the city, there shall a man meet you, bearing a pitcher of water; follow him into the house where he entereth in.

12
00:00:54.667 --> 00:01:03.467
And ye shall say unto the goodman of the house, The Master saith unto thee, Where is the guestchamber, where I shall eat the passover with my disciples?

13
00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:08.800
And he shall shew you a large upper room furnished: there make ready.

14
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.600
And they went, and found as he had said unto them: and they made ready the passover.

15
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.133
And when the hour was come, he sat down, and the twelve apostles with him.

16
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:30.400
And he said unto them, With desire I have desired to eat this passover with you before I suffer: For I say unto you, I will not any more eat thereof, until it be fulfilled in the kingdom of God.

17
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:40.933
And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and said, Take this, and divide it among yourselves: For I say unto you, I will not drink of the fruit of the vine, until the kingdom of God shall come.

18
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:50.000
And he took bread, and gave thanks, and brake it, and gave unto them, saying, This is my body which is given for you: this do in remembrance of me.

19
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:57.333
Likewise also the cup after supper, saying, This cup is the new testament in my blood, which is shed for you.

20
00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:02.000
But, behold, the hand of him that betrayeth me is with me on the table.

21
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:08.400
And truly the Son of man goeth, as it was determined: but woe unto that man by whom he is betrayed!

22
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.467
And they began to inquire among themselves, which of them it was that should do this thing.

23
00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:17.600
And there was also a strife among them, which of them should be accounted the greatest.

24
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:26.267
And he said unto them, The kings of the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and they that exercise authority upon them are called benefactors.

25
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:36.400
But ye shall not be so: but he that is greatest among you, let him be as the younger; and he that is chief, as he that doth serve.

26
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.400
For whether is greater, he that sitteth at meat, or he that serveth?

27
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.667
is not he that sitteth at meat?

28
00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:45.867
but I am among you as he that serveth.

29
00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:49.733
Ye are they which have continued with me in my temptations.

30
00:02:49.733 --> 00:03:01.333
And I appoint unto you a kingdom, as my Father hath appointed unto me; That ye may eat and drink at my table in my kingdom, and sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Israel.

31
00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:14.800
And the Lord said, Simon, Simon, behold, Satan hath desired to have you, that he may sift you as wheat: But I have prayed for thee, that thy faith fail not: and when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren.

32
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.267
And he said unto him, Lord, I am ready to go with thee, both into prison, and to death.

33
00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:28.933
And he said, I tell thee, Peter, the cock shall not crow this day, before that thou shalt thrice deny that thou knowest me.

34
00:03:28.933 --> 00:03:35.733
And he said unto them, When I sent you without purse, and scrip, and shoes, lacked ye any thing?

35
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:37.600
And they said, Nothing.

36
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:48.400
Then said he unto them, But now, he that hath a purse, let him take it, and likewise his scrip: and he that hath no sword, let him sell his garment, and buy one.

37
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:58.533
For I say unto you, that this that is written must yet be accomplished in me, And he was reckoned among the transgressors: for the things concerning me have an end.

38
00:03:58.533 --> 00:04:01.600
And they said, Lord, behold, here are two swords.

39
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.267
And he said unto them, It is enough.

40
00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:10.133
And he came out, and went, as he was wont, to the mount of Olives; and his disciples also followed him.

41
00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:16.800
And when he was at the place, he said unto them, Pray that ye enter not into temptation.

42
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:29.067
And he was withdrawn from them about a stone's cast, and kneeled down, and prayed, Saying, Father, if thou be willing, remove this cup from me: nevertheless not my will, but thine, be done.

43
00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:33.600
And there appeared an angel unto him from heaven, strengthening him.

44
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:41.600
And being in an agony he prayed more earnestly: and his sweat was as it were great drops of blood falling down to the ground.

45
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:50.400
And when he rose up from prayer, and was come to his disciples, he found them sleeping for sorrow, And said unto them, Why sleep ye?

46
00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.600
rise and pray, lest ye enter into temptation.

47
00:04:53.600 --> 00:05:03.200
And while he yet spake, behold a multitude, and he that was called Judas, one of the twelve, went before them, and drew near unto Jesus to kiss him.

48
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.867
But Jesus said unto him, Judas, betrayest thou the Son of man with a kiss?

49
00:05:07.867 --> 00:05:13.600
When they which were about him saw what would follow, they said unto him, Lord, shall we smite with the sword?

50
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.867
And one of them smote the servant of the high priest, and cut off his right ear.

51
00:05:17.867 --> 00:05:21.067
And Jesus answered and said, Suffer ye thus far.

52
00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.333
And he touched his ear, and healed him.

53
00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:33.067
Then Jesus said unto the chief priests, and captains of the temple, and the elders, which were come to him, Be ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and staves?

54
00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:40.667
When I was daily with you in the temple, ye stretched forth no hands against me: but this is your hour, and the power of darkness.

55
00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:45.467
Then took they him, and led him, and brought him into the high priest's house.

56
00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:47.733
And Peter followed afar off.

57
00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:55.067
And when they had kindled a fire in the midst of the hall, and were set down together, Peter sat down among them.

58
00:05:55.067 --> 00:06:02.667
But a certain maid beheld him as he sat by the fire, and earnestly looked upon him, and said, This man was also with him.

59
00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:07.067
And he denied him, saying, Woman, I know him not.

60
00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:11.867
And after a little while another saw him, and said, Thou art also of them.

61
00:06:11.867 --> 00:06:15.067
And Peter said, Man, I am not.

62
00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:24.667
And about the space of one hour after another confidently affirmed, saying, Of a truth this fellow also was with him: for he is a Galilaean.

63
00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:28.667
And Peter said, Man, I know not what thou sayest.

64
00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:31.600
And immediately, while he yet spake, the cock crew.

65
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.400
And the Lord turned, and looked upon Peter.

66
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:40.933
And Peter remembered the word of the Lord, how he had said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.

67
00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.600
And Peter went out, and wept bitterly.

68
00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.533
And the men that held Jesus mocked him, and smote him.

69
00:06:46.533 --> 00:06:54.133
And when they had blindfolded him, they struck him on the face, and asked him, saying, Prophesy, who is it that smote thee?

70
00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:57.867
And many other things blasphemously spake they against him.

71
00:06:57.867 --> 00:07:07.067
And as soon as it was day, the elders of the people and the chief priests and the scribes came together, and led him into their council, saying, Art thou the Christ?

72
00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:08.000
tell us.

73
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:16.133
And he said unto them, If I tell you, ye will not believe: And if I also ask you, ye will not answer me, nor let me go.

74
00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:20.400
Hereafter shall the Son of man sit on the right hand of the power of God.

75
00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.000
Then said they all, Art thou then the Son of God?

76
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.467
And he said unto them, Ye say that I am.

77
00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:30.533
And they said, What need we any further witness?

78
00:07:30.533 --> 00:07:33.333
for we ourselves have heard of his own mouth.

